terraform-github-tacos plans OpenTofu or Terraform in a pull request, applies it when a GitHub environment approves, then merges. It does what Terraform Cloud's VCS workflow does, with GitHub Actions alone.

The flow applies before the merge. Approving the deployment is the apply, and the pull request merges once the apply has succeeded, so the default branch never holds a change that was not applied.

The repository has two parts:

* [[Workflow|A GitHub Action]], called once per job of your workflow.
* [[Module|An OpenTofu module]] that creates the environments the apply waits on.
